## 10. Implementation Sequence for Cursor

### Phase 1: Infrastructure (do first)

1. Install dependencies: `pnpm add next-mdx-remote gray-matter reading-time`
2. Create `src/lib/content.ts` (content loading utility)
3. Create `src/app/sitemap.ts` and `src/app/robots.ts`
4. Create empty content directory structure: `src/content/blog/{en,fr}/` and `src/content/vs/{en,fr}/`
5. Merge new translation keys into `en.json` and `fr.json`

### Phase 2: Blog Pages

1. Create `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/blog/page.tsx` (blog index)
2. Create `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` (article page)
3. Style the blog article layout with Tailwind `prose` classes
4. Add article end-CTA component (reusable across all articles)
5. Add `@tailwindcss/typography` plugin if not already installed: `pnpm add -D @tailwindcss/typography`

### Phase 3: Comparison Pages

1. Create `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)/vs/[competitor]/page.tsx`
2. Create `src/components/marketing/sections/comparison-table.tsx` (reusable)
3. Create `src/components/marketing/sections/vs-cta.tsx` (reusable)

### Phase 4: Static Page SEO Updates

1. Update `generateMetadata` in every existing marketing page.tsx to use the metadata translation keys
2. Add `hreflang` alternates to every page's metadata
3. Add JSON-LD structured data to homepage, features, pricing, about
4. Create or add static OG image at `public/og-default.png`

### Phase 5: Content (I'll generate these in separate chats)

1. Write `.mdx` files for each article (EN first, then FR)
2. Write `.mdx` files for each comparison page (EN first, then FR)
3. Add featured images to `public/blog/`

